# Never open plugin-cache files

Do **not** open, Read, Grep, Write, reveal, or keep visible any file under
`.cursor/plugins/cache`. Especially never open `validate-drawio.sh`.

Forbidden:

- `open_resource` / `open_automation` on plugin-cache paths
- Read/Write/Grep of `validate-drawio.sh` or other cache helper scripts
- Navigating the editor to those tabs
- Using the AWS draw.io validator as a visible editor file

## Every chat response (hard)

**Before finishing every reply**, close any editor tab named `validate-drawio.sh`
or under `.cursor/plugins/cache`. Do this even when the user did not mention
it. The AWS draw.io plugin reopens that cache file on its own.

Do **not** Read/Grep/`open_resource` the file to check it. Close the tab only.

Windows: run the sibling PLC script (does not open the file; keeps Hub
`:8001` / `home.html`):

```text
powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File ..\electramet_plc\BuildScripts\Close-PluginCacheTabs.ps1
```

If that path is missing: UIA-select the `validate-drawio` TabItem, then its
Close button or Ctrl+W. Never close Hub Simple Browser (`home.html?hubCursor=1`).

Run any needed draw.io validator in the **shell** only, never in the editor.
